  "notes": [
    "Use ordinary connected terrain in the 80\u00d725 zone except these fixed physical supports; the old central-only walkable polygon was a conservative browser study and excluded visible side ledges.",
    "Seven loose rock props provide dynamic single-cell blocking; plants can remain passable but interactable. Every mutable contact cell has independent cardinal access even if all 39 props are treated as solid.",
    "Fixed structures are persistent and indestructible, not ordinary 40HP destructible Wall objects. Tall sprite silhouettes do not all block movement.",
    "Blackwater marks the deep channel; its polygon begins below the waterfall pool. The head pool remains a shallow traversable crossing joining the west bank to the side ledge. Use native liquid depths there if available; do not silently classify the whole stream bank as impassable water.",
    "The northern midpoint is inside the giant trunk. Existing inward arrival search can land south of the trunk; the north edge itself stays usable via the outer side margins.",
    "All six visible scar positions and the seventh wrong-air point use layout.json source-aligned coordinates. No historical identities or compass order are implied."
  ],
